(NATIVECAM SPOILBOARD SURFACING: 12 x 12 in, 2 passes of 0.02 in {0.04 in in all} with 1-1/4in)
(Surfacing Bit, 21 lines along X 0.6 in apart, both ways.)
(BED CLEAR: remove every clamp. Every screw head and T-nut must sit at least 0.125 in below the cut.)
(Set the dust shoe high enough for the surfacing bit's collet and the 0.5 in clearance.)
(Re-zero Z on the board before every run: each run takes 0.04 in off the surface it is zeroed on.)
(Runs about 4 min.)
